silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_05_relator_quotient_projection_sections_01_relator_to_congruence_closure_concrete_anchor_16_PathLawhceqgfc#pathlaw_h_c_eq_g_f_c silm:hasLongDescription "The PathLaw_h_c_eq_g_f_c is the commuting path equation: direct Animal leg equals the Cat->Mammal->Animal composite. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'PathLaw_h_c_eq_g_f_c', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
